        },
        {
          "_comment": "Correlation group example, 1 of 2: the primary. Every member of a group is its own top-level result, so the file holds one result for each open finding. Group membership is recorded in the result's own properties (correlation-group, correlation-role, correlation-primary), and the message ends with one sentence, after the control status, that names the group and the peers (up to 10, then a count). Neither is identity: a regroup changes the text and the properties and never a key. relatedLocations holds this finding's own control evidence only, and no entry names a finding.",
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "<threat-description-for-correlation-group-primary> [Control: partial] Correlated in CG-1; peers T-6.",
            "markdown": "<mitigation-recommendation-for-correlation-group-primary>"
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "<repo-relative-architecture-file-path>"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "<primary-component-name>",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "<trust-zone>/<primary-component-name>",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "relatedLocations": [
            {
              "id": 0,
              "message": {
                "text": "Control evidence: <control-category> detected in <file-path>"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "<control-evidence-file-path>"
                },
                "region": {
